        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "New Jazz Underground is worth tracking because the trio does not treat tradition and contemporary language as opposing camps: Armenteros, Rios and Reddick can swing hard, leave real improvisational space, and then let hip-hop or Afro-Latin rhythmic ideas reshape the same conversation. Hoodies gives the group a current body of original material, while The Pocket puts a sax-bass-drums trio in exactly the kind of small room where chemistry and time feel exposed rather than packaged.",
          "trip_verdict": "Worth catching if New York is already in play today. At this late point in the day I would not build a fresh DMV-to-NYC trip around it, but the trio belongs on the RADAR and is an easy yes if you are already nearby and one of the two sets fits.",
